  era: "Section 4 \xB7 Religious Movements \xB7 6th \u2013 5th century BCE onwards"
  title: Spread of Buddhism
  text: Royal patronage, especially from Ashoka, together with monasteries, trade routes and missionaries, carried Buddhism to Sri Lanka, Central Asia, China and South-East Asia. Great monasteries such as Nalanda became centres of learning.
